Track 1: Tidal Locks Swallow the Lead
- Story & Context: When Silas Vance dragged a rusted iron chest full of 1880s clockmaker tools and a fallen meteorite out of the Whitby mudflats, he immediately built the bridge pins for Kaelen’s custom melodica. Recording inside an abandoned lighthouse during a high-tide storm, they tracked the instrument's first breathy, looping notes over a sub-bass rumble that literally cracked the damp plaster on the walls. The track captured the exact moment the scene's signature sound was born, bridging old maritime iron with modern low-end warmth. "The water steps inside the gear, and now we drift away," Kaelen sang into a wet ribbon microphone as the tide knocked on the heavy wooden doors.
